  "version": 1,
  "title": "Near-linear cycles in connected vertex-transitive graphs",
  "abstract": "A Lean formalization of the near-linear cycle theorem in \"Lovász conjecture holds asymptotically\". For every positive ε, sufficiently large connected finite vertex-transitive graphs contain a simple cycle with at least n^(1−ε) edges. The development includes a weaker-constant Bondy–Locke path-to-cycle comparison and the finite approximate-group and expansion arguments used in the path proofs.",
